inding":"The streak-counter reset transition is unreachable on the code path where it must fire: reclaim_under_pressure early-returns at autodeploy.sh:302 when pct < DISK_PRESSURE_PCT, before any post-reclaim streak logic. The AC requires the counter to 'reset to zero once the disk falls below the threshold', but that below-threshold tick takes the early return, so a reset placed near the increment (post-reclaim) never executes.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f7aa142e63201708d","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Scope §3 / 'Persistence and configurability of the streak counter' / AC line 'increments … resets to zero once the disk falls below the threshold'","norm_id":"n799fc01a4fd66d58","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Disk is pressured for 4 cycles (streak=4, marker firing), then recovers below threshold; the next tick hits the :302 early return and never zeroes the counter, so the marker keeps firing on the next unrelated pressure blip"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"In reclaim_under_pressure, before the `pct < DISK_PRESSURE_PCT` early return, write 0 to PRESSURE_STREAK_FILE (tmp-then-mv); increment only after prune_docker_caches when the post-reclaim pct is still >= threshold.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"high"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Define the streak-counter behaviour on the throttled-but-pressured tick (autodeploy.sh:307-310): does the streak increment only on a completed reclaim, or per pressured tick regardless of throttle — and state which so the alarm latency is deterministic.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.4,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["autodeploy.sh:307-310 throttled branch `return 0` with no reclaim","PRESSURE_PRUNE_MIN_INTERVAL default 600s (:132) vs ~2-min timer ticks","Plan increment rule fires only 'when a reclaim completes'"],"finding":"The streak increment rule is unspecified for the throttled-but-pressured tick. reclaim_under_pressure runs prune_docker_caches only when NOT within PRESSURE_PRUNE_MIN_INTERVAL (autodeploy.sh:307-310); the plan's rule keys the increment on 'when a reclaim completes and the disk is STILL >= DISK_PRESSURE_PCT', which leaves the throttled path (pressure present, no reclaim run) undefined. With a 600s throttle against ~2-min ticks, the majority of pressured ticks are throttled, so this choice determines whether the streak counts reclaims (~10min per unit) or wall-clock persistence.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f8c5ad9e181216250","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Scope §3 / AC line 'When a reclaim completes and the disk is STILL at or above DISK_PRESSURE_PCT, the persisted streak counter increments'","norm_id":"n48ea3b0e3fd361f5","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Disk sits at 90% for 25 minutes; only ~2-3 un-throttled reclaims run in that window, so a streak keyed on reclaims reaches PRESSURE_STREAK_ALARM=3 at ~30min while a tick-based reading would reach it in ~6min — the operator's 'ineffective reclaim' signal latency depends entirely on this undefined choice"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"high"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify that a failed/refused `docker image rm` in the retire path is logged (retained-because-referenced vs error), so a silently-ineffective removal is observable.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5a","T5b","T5e"],"criteria":["T5b"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.075,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["\"Removal uses docker image rm WITHOUT -f, so the daemon itself refuses while any container still references the image\"","No AC or scope text states the rm-failure outcome is logged rather than ignored"],"finding":"The plan does not specify how a failed 'docker image rm' (the daemon refusing because another container still references the image, or any other error) is handled — whether it is logged or silently swallowed.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fbf5a81028ac1549c",